<% content_for :title, "Lee Powell - Founder of Wrap My Cover" %>
<% content_for :description, "Lee Powell is the author, founder and software engineer behind Wrap My Cover and Lumen & Lever's traceable AI document systems." %>

<% content_for :head do %>
  <% canonical_root = "https://#{ApplicationController::CANONICAL_HOST || request.host}" %>
  <% profile_schema = {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "ProfilePage",
    "@id": "#{canonical_root}/founder#profile",
    "url": "#{canonical_root}/founder",
    "name": "Lee Powell - Founder of Wrap My Cover",
    "mainEntity": { "@id": "#{canonical_root}/#lee-powell" }
  } %>
  <script type="application/ld+json" nonce="<%= content_security_policy_nonce %>">
    <%= raw json_escape(profile_schema.to_json) %>
  </script>
<% end %>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-16 pb-12">
  <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-oxblood-600">Founder</p>
  <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl text-balance">
    Lee Powell builds writing, publishing and AI systems that have to hold up.
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg text-parchment-700">
    Lee Powell is an author, founder and software engineer in Melbourne. He built
    document software used by writers worldwide, including Scrivener and Scapple for
    Windows, and founded Lumen & Lever to build traceable AI and document systems for
    production work.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-semibold">
    <%= link_to "Lee Powell author site", "https://leepowell.com",
          class: "rounded-lg border border-parchment-300 px-4 py-2 text-parchment-900 hover:bg-parchment-100" %>
    <%= link_to "Lumen & Lever", "https://lumenandlever.com",
          class: "rounded-lg border border-parchment-300 px-4 py-2 text-parchment-900 hover:bg-parchment-100" %>
    <%= link_to "GitHub keny369", "https://github.com/keny369",
          class: "rounded-lg border border-parchment-300 px-4 py-2 text-parchment-900 hover:bg-parchment-100" %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-parchment-200 bg-parchment-100/60 py-14">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-8 px-5 md:grid-cols-3">
    <article>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Author</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-parchment-700">
        Lee writes books and field guides about systems, agency and the traps people get
        caught inside. Wrap My Cover was built from a working author's print-production
        problem, not as a generic graphics demo.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Software engineer</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-parchment-700">
        His work spans document software, banking and government systems, retail platforms
        and production services where calculation, auditability and operational boundaries
        matter.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Founder</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-parchment-700">
        Through Lumen & Lever, Lee builds practical AI systems for documents and decisions:
        source-traced answers, reviewable outputs and workflows that expose what the model
        used rather than hiding it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Why this matters for Wrap My Cover</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-parchment-700">
    KDP cover generation is a production problem: the math has to be current, the PDF has
    to be exact, and authors need to know what changed when trim, paper, binding or page
    count changes. The project carries Lee's wider systems approach into a narrow, useful
    publishing tool.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5">
    <%= link_to "Read the case studies", case_studies_path,
          class: "font-semibold text-parchment-900 underline-offset-4 hover:underline" %>
  </p>
</section>

